# P0 fixes — 2026-07-14

Applied to the working tree and verified green. NOT committed: the files they touch are part of
the paused Codex in-flight work (agent_images.py and agent_telemetry.py are not even tracked in
git yet), so committing would sweep up ~88k lines that are not mine. Land the Codex batch first,
then these go on top as a small, reviewable diff.

## Fixes and their tests (all new tests are mine and pass)

1. Safe Mode fail-open across the desktop <-> MCP process boundary
   - crossage_fr/enroll/manager.py : ProjectState.refresh_config_from_disk() (stat-guarded re-read)
   - crossage_fr/agent_images.py   : _safe_mode_status() calls it at the enforcement boundary
   - test: tests/safe_mode_cross_process_units.py

2. Telemetry on by default + plaintext trace log shipped in backups
   - crossage_fr/agent_telemetry.py : MCP_OTEL_ENABLED default False (opt-in)
   - crossage_fr/enroll/manager.py  : export_workspace_backup excludes the trace log
   - mcp/README.md                  : documents tracing as opt-in, never in backups
   - test: tests/telemetry_default_off_units.py

3. Moving/renaming a file destroyed its identity (live data loss)
   - crossage_fr/store/workspace_db.py : _photo_asset_id_for_moved_file() content-hash rehoming,
     guarded by content_hash AND file signature (size+mtime) AND old-path-gone AND single-candidate.
     The signature guard is what makes it safe: "path missing" is not proof of a move (external drive
     unplugged), so a copy imported from a backup must not hijack the vanished asset.
   - test: tests/asset_identity_rehome_units.py

4. Hidden / Recently-Deleted assets reachable by a paired phone that knows the asset id
   - crossage_fr/agent_images.py : _metadata_restricts_agent_access() filtered in _hydrate_assets
     (covers fetch_assets + analyze_assets) and checked in preview(). Reported as "not found", never
     "forbidden", so it is not an existence oracle.
   - test: tests/agent_hidden_asset_gate_units.py

5. Warm-cache workspace-lock bypass on the mobile/MCP surface
   - crossage_fr/mcp_server.py : _image_service() calls _assert_unlocked() UNCONDITIONALLY (per
     request), not only at singleton construction. Before this, a phone paired while unlocked kept
     reading the library after the user enabled + locked Workspace Lock; and the no-consent
     capabilities() route was never lock-gated at all. Confirmed independently by the trace workflow,
     which recommended this exact root fix.
   - test: tests/mcp_workspace_lock_warm_cache_units.py

6. Cross-machine backup restore was impossible (disaster-recovery ship-blocker)
   - crossage_fr/enroll/manager.py : restore/verify treated a cross-machine SQLCipher key mismatch as
     an uncaught WorkspaceEncryptionError and aborted before extracting a file. Now the backup manifest
     records workspaceKeyId, and verify distinguishes a genuine key mismatch (host key id != archived
     key id -> recoverable, restore proceeds) from corruption (key id matches but the DB won't open ->
     hard fail). Same-machine full integrity checking is unchanged.
   - test: tests/workspace_backup_cross_machine_units.py

7. Preview API advertised maxPreviewDimension=2048 but silently returned 768 (PIL.thumbnail never
   upscales, and the base image was always the 768px list thumbnail).
   - crossage_fr/enroll/manager.py : preview_path_for(...)/_preview_cache_path(...) accept a max_edge
     (default 768, so existing callers and caches are byte-identical); larger previews are generated
     from the original and cached per-edge.
   - crossage_fr/agent_images.py   : preview() requests the base preview at the dimension it serves.
     Honest up to the source's own resolution; small originals are not upscaled.
   - test: tests/preview_dimension_honesty_units.py

8. "Catalog-only" Open Photo Catalog export still shipped media bytes (Live Photo .mov halves, depth
   maps, RAW/XMP companions) when include_sidecars was true (the default) — a privacy + size surprise.
   - crossage_fr/photo_catalog_portability.py : sidecar byte export now requires include_originals;
     catalog-only ships zero media bytes and the manifest reports includeSidecars truthfully. The
     pairing relationship is still exported as photo_media_pairs metadata rows.
   - test: tests/catalog_only_no_media_bytes_units.py

Dispositioned (NOT spot-fixed, with reasons) — see 2026-07-14-remaining-work-disposition.md:
  - B14 keyword LWW data loss: correct fix is an OR-Set (wire-format v1->v2); a partial CRDT would be
    wrong. Belongs to E1.1. local_sync.py is dormant.
  - E0.7 SQLite contention: empirically the RLock serializes ALL in-process connections; the correct
    fix is connection pooling + RLock-scope reduction, validatable only under concurrent load. Not a
    safe blind change on churned workspace_db.py.
  - E0.1 canonical asset_uid, E0.6 serial loop, and the mobile app itself (E1-E3): net-new build work.
  - LAN bind / Info.plist / recovery UI / consent gate: Electron/native, unverifiable in this env.

## Corrected (claims from the audit / spec that tracing overturned)

- "A paired phone bypasses the workspace lock." Half wrong. The COLD-process claim is false
  (_api() -> _assert_unlocked() fails closed). But the WARM-cache path was a real bug (fix 5).
- "Recovery is decorative / the Emergency Kit cannot open the backup." WRONG at the crypto layer:
  the scrypt+AES-GCM recovery envelope is bundled in the ZIP and the printed code alone opens the
  inner SQLCipher DB (proven end-to-end). The real bug was the cross-machine restore crash (fix 6).
- "SecureEnclave can hold the Ed25519/X25519 identity." FALSE — CryptoKit exposes only
  SecureEnclave.P256. Recorded in the recovery design; no code depends on it yet.

